      },
      "writtenOn": "2013-07-23T02:35:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could go either way but i would say no, stick with PUT. \n\nWhen i perform a POST to a location i expect it to create a new record. eg POST /customer creates a customer later accessible at /customer/customerid (sticking with a non-keystone example as it is a restful idea rather than something that keystone necessarily does)\n\nAs this is later accessible at the same location i\u0027d classify that an in place operation and thus a PUT",
